Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:55:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Qt client: size the Freeciv45 unit bar to its action boxes

The bar was one row: portrait, a text column and a column of chips over
actions, as wide as all of them side by side (467 to 495 points). It is
now a column: the portrait with the unit's name, rank and city, moves and
hit points, and strength on four short lines; the tile mates' chips under
that; then the action boxes. The width is that of the action boxes, or of
the unit's lines or the chip row when those are wider, up to six boxes. A
seventh box wraps onto another row instead of widening the bar, and so do
chips. Nothing is reserved for actions or chips that are not there: a
unit alone on its tile shows no chip, since its portrait is the unit.
Lines wider than the room are cut with an ellipsis and carry the whole
text as a tooltip. The portrait is 56 points, not 80.

With four actions the bar is 198 points wide and 152 high, from 467 by
98; with five and a stack of five, 228 by 160, from 495 by 98.

Issue 233.
